{#- Dessert fridge sign (client 2026-10-29): black & white, no logo, just
    the prices. Every dessert in the fridge is one price since that day
    (cheesecake, cream puffs, whatever the batch is), so the sign names
    none of them: they change with each batch. That price is Cheesecake's
    in menu.json and the bars' is Dessert Bar's (its kinds are the magic
    bar and the rice crispy treat); a dessert added from the kitchen
    board's Manage -> Desserts lives only in Square, so set it to the same
    price there. If you find yourself typing a price here, stop. -#}
{%- set desserts = (menu.categories | where("id", "desserts"))[0] %}
{%- set fridge = (desserts.items | where("name", "Cheesecake"))[0] %}
{%- set bars = (desserts.items | where("name", "Dessert Bar"))[0] %}
<div class="canvas sign sign--bw fd">
    <div class="sign-heading">
        <h2 class="p-display sign-heading-title">Desserts</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="fd-items">
        {%- if fridge %}
        <section class="fd-item">
            <p class="p-display fd-name">Fridge Desserts</p>
            <p class="fd-sub">Any dessert in this fridge</p>
            <p class="p-display fd-price">{{ fridge.price | money }} <span class="fd-each">each</span></p>
        </section>
        {%- endif %}

        {%- if bars %}
        <section class="fd-item">
            <p class="p-display fd-name">Magic Bars &amp;<br>Rice Crispy Treats</p>
            <p class="p-display fd-price">{{ bars.price | money }} <span class="fd-each">each</span></p>
        </section>
        {%- endif %}
    </div>
</div>
